{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "abfade58-c11a-876e-b18a-8108409ed98f",
  "created_at": "2026-02-18T15:31:40-05:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, Public Works",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Bruce Chase",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Denise Arruda",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-18T15:27:07-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Public Works, this is Denise."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-18T15:27:10-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Hello, yes, good afternoon. I'm sorry to bother you. Is this the right place to ask about trash and recycling?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-18T15:27:20-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "It sure is. What can I help you with?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-18T15:27:25-05:00",
      "duration": 17,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Well, I have a few questions about what goes in the recycling now. I heard the rules changed, and I want to be sure I'm doing it right. I don't want to put the wrong things out."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-18T15:27:42-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Sure, go ahead. What are you wondering about?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-18T15:27:46-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Pizza boxes first. Can those go in the recycling bin? Even if there's a little grease on them?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-18T15:27:55-05:00",
      "duration": 17,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Greasy pizza boxes are a problem. If the box is clean, or you tear off the clean top and recycle that, fine. The part with grease and cheese stuck on it should go in the trash."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-18T15:28:12-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. So the clean top can go in, and the greasy bottom goes in the trash. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-18T15:28:21-05:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "That's right."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-18T15:28:23-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Good, thank you. And glass? Jars and bottles? I've been putting them in, but I wasn't certain I should be."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-18T15:28:33-05:00",
      "duration": 15,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Glass bottles and jars are fine in the curbside recycling. Rinse them out, and you can leave the labels on. Just no broken glass, no drinking glasses, and no window glass."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-18T15:28:48-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Rinsed, labels can stay, no broken glass or drinking glasses. Let me make sure I have that. Rinsed jars and bottles only."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-18T15:28:59-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yep, you've got it."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-18T15:29:02-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "And the last one is those plastic clamshells. The ones the berries and the salad come in. Do those go in?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-18T15:29:12-05:00",
      "duration": 20,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Those are usually okay if they're the hard, rigid plastic with a recycling number on them. Empty them, give them a quick rinse, and put them in loose. Don't bag them. The thin, flimsy film stuff and plastic bags go in the trash."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-18T15:29:32-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Loose, not in a bag. All right. I'm sorry, I keep asking you to repeat things."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-18T15:29:40-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Not at all, that's what I'm here for. Better to ask than guess."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-18T15:29:47-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Thank you. Now, when is my next pickup? I'm at 249 Rhode Island Avenue."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-18T15:29:54-05:00",
      "duration": 14,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Rhode Island Avenue, up on the Hill. Let me pull that up. [pause] Okay, one moment while it loads. Do you know what day you usually get picked up?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-18T15:30:08-05:00",
      "duration": 18,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I think it's Thursday, but I'm not sure. I work some weekends, so I lose track of the days. I pick up extra weekend hours so we can afford a family trip this spring, and everything runs together."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-18T15:30:26-05:00",
      "duration": 17,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Well, that sounds worth it. Okay, I see your address. Trash goes out Thursday, which is tomorrow. Recycling goes out on alternating weeks, and this week is a recycling week, so both would go out tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-18T15:30:43-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Both tomorrow. So I should put them out tonight or in the morning?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-18T15:30:50-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Tonight is fine, or early tomorrow morning. Crews start early, so I'd have it at the curb before seven."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-18T15:30:59-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Before seven, at the curb. And recycling is tomorrow, too, you said? I want to be sure, since I don't want to miss it."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-18T15:31:10-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, tomorrow, Thursday. Trash and recycling both. After that, recycling is every other week."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-18T15:31:17-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Every other week, all right. I'll write that down. Thank you very much, and sorry again for the trouble."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-18T15:31:26-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No trouble at all, Mr. Chase. Anything else I can help with today?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-18T15:31:33-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No, that's everything. Thank you. Goodbye."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-18T15:31:37-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You take care. Bye now."
    }
  ],
